# Nourished Mod — Cline Rules
# These rules apply to every session in this repo.

## Commit Message Format

Always write commit messages in Conventional Commits format:

```
<type>(<scope>): <short description>
```

### Types

| Type       | When to use                                              |
|------------|----------------------------------------------------------|
| `feat`     | New feature or behaviour visible to players              |
| `fix`      | Bug fix                                                  |
| `perf`     | Performance improvement (caching, fewer ticks, etc)      |
| `refactor` | Code restructure with no behaviour change                |
| `compat`   | Mod compatibility — new compat entries or fixes          |
| `content`  | New food tags, items, recipes, advancements              |
| `tags`     | Bulk tag file additions (nutrient category tag files)    |
| `docs`     | README, wiki, in-code comments only                      |
| `chore`    | Build config, .gitignore, tooling — never shown in changelog |
| `ci`       | GitHub Actions / workflow changes only                   |

### Scopes (use the relevant package or system name)

`memory`, `hud`, `screen`, `network`, `decay`, `effects`, `scanner`,
`compat`, `config`, `tags`, `command`, `registry`, `attachment`

### Rules

- **Always use a scope** when the change is isolated to one system
- **Description is lowercase**, no trailing period, imperative mood ("add" not "added")
- **Be specific** — describe what changed, not that something was "enhanced" or "updated"
- **Never write** `Update changelog [skip ci]` — the CI handles changelog automatically
- **Never write** vague messages like "fix bug", "update code", "refactor stuff"

### Good examples

```
feat(memory): add exponential decay curves to food memory entries
fix(hud): correct drag bounds clipping on ultrawide resolutions
perf(scanner): cache FoodFamilyResolver lookups in ConcurrentHashMap
compat(farmersdelight): tag 47 new items across proteins and grains
tags(vegetables): add 23 Croptopia vegetable items
refactor(network): split SyncDietPayload into full and delta variants
fix(effects): replace player.tickCount with level().getGameTime()
feat(screen): add active effects panel to DietScreen
```

### Bad examples (never write these)

```
Update changelog [skip ci]        ← CI does this, never manual
Enhance food scanning             ← too vague
Fix bug                           ← which bug?
Update diet screen                ← what changed?
misc changes                      ← not conventional commits
```

